  "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ if $y={5}^{x}sec\u2061x.$",
  "worked_solution": "We calculate the derivative using the product rule, as follows:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({5}^{x}sec\u2061x) \\\\  & ={5}^{x}ln\u20615sec\u2061x+{5}^{x}sec\u2061xtan\u2061x \\\\  & ={5}^{x}sec\u2061x(ln\u20615+tan\u2061x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
